  "title": "Benin brass plaques of the Oba’s palace",
  "summary": "Cast by royal brasscasters of the Edo people, the Benin plaques are brass reliefs that decorated the walls and columns of the Oba’s palace in Benin City; nearly 900 once decorated the palace courtyard. Museums date them to the late 16th to 17th centuries. After the 1897 siege of Benin, plaques were sent to England and entered museum collections.",
